4. Baseline's Unique Value Proposition (UVP)
Where Baseline truly outshines the competition is its intersection of Enterprise Rigor and Modern SaaS Agility:

The "True Project Manager's" Modern Tool: While Asana and Monday are built for general workers, Baseline provides actual PM methodology tools (EVM, RACI, Risk Logs) without the clunky, outdated interfaces of legacy software like MS Project or Primavera.
Global Economic Fairness: Your implementation of localized, regional discounts (Purchasing Power Parity) is incredibly rare in B2B SaaS. This gives Baseline a massive competitive edge in emerging markets (Africa, LATAM, Southeast Asia) where tools like Jira and Asana are prohibitively expensive in USD.
Hybrid Reality: Most companies claim to be Agile, but actually operate in a Hybrid/Waterfall environment. Baseline acknowledges this reality and supports both natively without forcing a paradigm shift.
TIP

Strategic Recommendation for Go-To-Market Lean heavily into marketing to Agencies, Consultancies, and Hybrid Tech/Hardware companies in emerging markets. Highlight your Regional Pricing and your EVM/RACI tools. These are demographics that are currently deeply underserved and overcharged by Asana and Atlassian.


